BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hardly Strictly Irish Harvest Moon Concert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T183000
UID:260925wniYFCslbEukeLHaqBYm0w
DESCRIPTION:**Hardly Strictly Irish Harvest Moon Concert & Potluck/Dance P
 arty**\n\nSeptember 26\, 2026\n\nConcert 5:00-6:30 p.m. | Potluck After-Pa
 rty 6:30-7:30 p.m.\n\n**TICKETS:** **$25 General / $20 Seniors & Youth** |
  **At The Door $35 General / $30 Seniors & Youth (doors at 4:30 p.m.)**\n\
 n**Hardly Strictly Irish** (Suzuki Cady and Jimmy Murphy) bring an uplifti
 ng\, warm\, and soulful energy\, and a signature blend of traditional Iris
 h tunes and Appalachian\, country-folk\, and roots-Americana songs. Their 
 rich sound features the fiddle\, mandolin\, guitar\, banjo\, bodhrán\, an
 d vocal harmonies.\n\n**Shiloh Step Irish Dance** will perform and teach a
  Ceili (group dance) after the show\, for anyone interested. Bring a potlu
 ck dish (optional) to share after the show in honor of the Harvest Moon!\n
 \nThe venue is beautiful\, with great acoustics\, comfortable seats\, room
  to dance\, and easy parking! And a lovely fountain garden area with seati
 ng to enjoy after the show.\n\nSt. Stephen’s Sanctuary\, 500 Robinson Ro
 ad\, Sebastopol CA\n\nMore information: http://suzukicady.com/tix\n\nAdvan
 ce Tickets: https://tixfox.co/e/harvestmoon
LOCATION:St. Stephen's Sanctuary
URL:https://tixfox.co/e/harvestmoon
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Heart & Mind Equine Rescue: Self-Compassion with Horses
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T103000
UID:2609258JTk7jfua0OfGalrg-cChQ
DESCRIPTION:Offered by Heart & Mind Equine Rescue. Meet our rescued therap
 y horses\, explore our volunteer program\, and learn about holistic horse 
 keeping and equine-assisted services \\(e.g.\, therapy\, coaching\, leader
 ship\, and team building with horses\\). No experience is necessary. All a
 re welcome\, including both horse and mental health professionals.\n\nWhat
  would it feel like to offer yourself the same kindness and care you so fr
 eely give to others?\n\nJoin Alane Freund and the Heart & Mind Equine herd
  for Self-Compassion with Horses\, a 90-minute experiential session design
 ed to help you slow down\, become present\, and reconnect with yourself.\n
 \nThrough mindfulness\, reflection\, and guided experiences with the horse
 s\, we’ll explore self-compassion\, self-awareness\, grounding\, and aut
 hentic connection.\n\nHorses naturally invite us into the present moment. 
 Their sensitivity and responsiveness can help us notice what we’re feeli
 ng\, soften self-criticism\, and practice meeting ourselves with greater k
 indness and curiosity.\n\nWhat to Expect\n\n• Guided experiences with th
 e horses • Mindfulness and grounding • Reflection and self-compassion 
 practices • Connection in a supportive\, welcoming environment\n\nNo hor
 se experience is necessary. All activities are ground-based.\n\nCome as yo
 u are and spend a morning practicing a little more kindness toward yoursel
 f.\n\nSpace is limited. Reserve your place today.\n\nCurious about Equine 
 Assisted Services? Horse Rescue Class is not therapy\, but it is an opport
 unity to get a “taste” of our work with our equine colleagues since we
  use some of the same tools and exercises in both settings. Come out and m
 eet the herd \\(both humans and horses\\) connected with Heart & Mind Equi
 ne.\n\nEach month\, the class is centered on a theme such as holistic hors
 e keeping\, equine-assisted learning\, understanding herd dynamics\, holis
 tic horse care and training\, and how these all relate to our human journe
 y.\n\nNature or horse lovers\, high achievers living with stress\, spiritu
 al seekers\, highly sensitive people\, mental health providers\, parents\,
  and teachers might especially benefit from this class as well as horse ow
 ners/riders who hope to improve their relationships with their equine part
 ners. \\(Though this work is great for dogs as well\, your dogs are not we
 lcome at our horse rescue due to liability and distraction concerns.\\) Ne
 wcomers and novices are most welcome. Service dogs do not usually do well 
 at the barn\, but please email to discuss.\n\nCome and experience the magi
 c of working with horses firsthand. Get ready to roll up your sleeves\, ge
 t your hands dirty\, and connect with these majestic creatures. Whether yo
 u're a seasoned equestrian or just starting out\, there's something for ev
 eryone at our Speaking Horse classes. Don't miss out on this exciting chan
 ce to bond with horses and fellow horse lovers. We can't wait to see you t
 here!\n\nChildren 9 and older are welcome with adult participation and sup
 ervision \\(and legal guardian signed liability release\\). Youth 15 and o
 lder may attend alone with a signed parental permission form. We meet in a
  pasture which has uneven ground and slippery gravel. For these reasons\, 
 we offer limited accommodation for participants with mobility challenges. 
 \\(We are able to offer some in-place\, chair-based experiences\, as well 
 as onsite parking\, so we invite those with challenges to reach out to lea
 rn more. Please call to RSVP 415-203-6600\, first come\, first served.\\)\
 n\nHolistic horse keeping methods and perspectives form the primary vision
  for our rescue. This class is a fundraiser for the nonprofit horse rescue
 \, so please donate what you can\, either here\, by VenMo\, or at the clas
 s. Note that Eventbrite will charge you a processing fee. Directions and l
 iability paperwork are sent upon registration. This is a volunteer orienta
 tion as well. It is an opportunity to meet our herd\, both horses and huma
 ns\, and find out if you might like to get involved. All registration fees
  are donations that support the rescue herd.\n\nRegister for directions to
  the barn.
LOCATION:Heart and Mind Equine
URL:https://areyouhighlysensitive.thrivecart.com/self-compassion-reboot/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
