BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Social Contractors - Live & Free @ Twin Oaks Roadhouse!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T160000
UID:260922Wq0eqlUHWU28er9ClhMJ1g
DESCRIPTION:“….Get ready for the super-entertaining sounds of local ba
 nd The Social Contractors. They totally rock\, in all the right ways…”
  - Argus-Courier\n\nJoin The Social Contractors at Twin Oaks Roadhouse for
  a lively afternoon of upbeat original rock plus their own spin on classic
  hits you know and love \\(e.g. Beatles\, CCR\, Hendrix\, Doors\, Pink Flo
 yd\, Police\, Men At Work\, U2\, Tears for Fears\, Tom Petty\, Steely Dan\
 , Foreigner\, Steve Miller\, and more\\)!\n\nWhether you enjoy melodic voc
 als\, searing guitar and sax solos\, intriguing lyrics\, captivating songs
 \, or just great dynamic and danceable rhythms\, The Social Contractors al
 ways deliver and never disappoint!\n\nThe lineup for this free live perfor
 mance features band founder and songwriter\, Jason E Davies \\(lead vocals
 \, lead/rhythm guitar\\)\, Travis Thayer \\(sax/keys/vocals\\)\, Rob Neide
 l \\(bass/vocals\\)\, and Chris Oatman \\(drums\\).\n\nAbout Twin Oaks Roa
 dhouse: Charm and character have accumulated at this very spot since 1926\
 , making the Twin Oaks a place where stories are told and made. Whatever y
 our definition of a tavern\, honky tonk or roadhouse\, rest assured there
 ’s a bit of each in here. Take a break travelers. There’s a bar\, a fi
 replace\, a kitchen\, a backyard and a dance floor.
LOCATION:Twin Oaks Roadhouse
URL:https://www.sonomacounty.com/food-drink/restaurants/twin-oaks-roadhous
 e/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:UC Master Gardeners Fall Faire
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T160000
UID:260922IjPrtxqMYkaiB45zIYjmxw
DESCRIPTION:**The UC Master Gardeners Fall Faire** is a **free**\, lively\
 , all ages event **from 1-4pm on Saturday\, September 26\,** with over 30 
 educational and community partner exhibits and hands-on demonstrations\, S
 carecrow Row\, an ornamental & winter veggie plant sale\, **special activi
 ties for kids**\, **including books\,** and so much more!   \n\nLearn ho
 w to dehydrate summer’s bounty\, create garlands from your garden\, take
  succulent clippings\, swap seeds and get seeds\, ask garden questions at 
 our Help Desk.  Hone your tool sharpening skills\, explore the Japanese A
 rt of Bonsai and the Napa Valley Orchid Society\, go native with the CA Na
 tive Plant Society\, learn about bees & bugs\, Firewise landscaping\, rose
 s\, healthy soils\, growing veggies year-round\, and more.\n\n**Annie's Lu
 nch Box food truck and the Big Ranch Rounders will offer food and entertai
 nment.** \n\n**Join us for this fun\, fall Faire!**\n\n**Location:** UC Ma
 ster Gardeners of Napa County\, 1710 Soscol Avenue\, Napa (near Central Va
 lley Hardware)\n\n**Date/Time:** Saturday\, September 26\, 1-4pm.
LOCATION:UC Master Gardeners of Napa County
URL:https://ucanr.edu/site/uc-master-gardeners-napa-county/event/napa-coun
 ty-master-gardeners-fall-faire
