BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Healdsburg Internation Short Film Festival 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T223000
UID:2609183Da-mvV9PEyGS5ibSUwNEw
DESCRIPTION:This three-day festival runs from September 25th through Sept
 ember 27th. Organized in collaboration with the **Healdsburg Center for t
 he Arts (HCA**)\, HISFF 2026 coincides with HCA’s **Festival of the Art
 s**\, creating a vibrant\, art-filled weekend.\n\nHISFF 2026 kicks off wi
 th an Opening Night Soirée\, a lively red-carpet arrival and photo op at
  the Raven\, and an exquisite collection of mixed genre short films. Festi
 vities continue with multiple screening sessions\, a Saturday night party 
 at **The Rooftop at the Harmon Guest House**\, and a filmmaker breakfast\
 , culminating in an awards ceremony on Sunday night.\n\nOur panel of notab
 le judges from the entertainment industry makes the HISFF an attraction fo
 r new and veteran filmmakers alike — people like **Ed Begley\, Jr.\, Lar
 aine Newman\, Billy Ray\, Tom Waits**\, and so many more. Several judges a
 re attending the festival this year\, including writer Billy Ray (*The Hun
 ger Games* and the soon-to-be released *The Hunger Games: Sunrise On the
  Reaping* )\, who will make a book-signing appearance at the Raven on Sat
 urday\, September 26th (Time TBD).\n\nVisit our booth at the Healdsburg F
 estival of the Arts on Saturday\, September 26th\, from 10 am to 6 pm on 
 Center Street in front of HCA (just steps away from the Raven). The street
  will be lined with booths featuring fine arts\, crafts\, jewelry\, poetry
 \, live music\, food trucks\, and more!\n\nCopperfield’s is organizing a
  free-admission book-signing event with screenwriter (and festival jurist)
  Billy Ray at the Raven from 11:00 am\, also on Saturday\, September 26th.
  Books will be available for purchase and signing\, but it’s best to ord
 er your copy ahead of time from Copperfield’s.\n\n**All Access Pass: $17
 5. Includes:**\n\n\\- Red-Carpet arrival and photo op begins at 6 pm at th
 e Raven.\n\n\\- Opening Night Kick-Off Screening Block\, 7:00 pm.\n\n\\- O
 pening Night Kick-Off Soirée\, 8:30 pm at Portalupi Wines.\n\n\\- Saturda
 y Night Sweet & Uncorked Social at the beautiful Harmon House Rooftop\, 8:
 15 pm.\n\n\\- Every screening session\, including the filmmaker Q&A sessio
 ns.
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/hisff2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:On Site Compost and Biochar Demonstration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T130000
UID:260917qsWqgyuhMkuSLCsFB5aMMQ
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for the first in a series of composti
 ng workshops taught by Bobby Nicholson of Compost Depot with the
  Sonoma Ecology Center (SEC) and Sonoma Biochar Initiative (SBI).
  The workshops are funded by Zero Waste Sonoma (ZWS) and free 
 to the public. The workshop series will continue with five on s
 ite compost workshops throughout Sonoma county. \n\nLet's get dirt
 y! The workshop will provide practical guidelines and accessible 
 soil science to build a healthy composting program on location w
 ith available resources and using a scalable model. Raymond Balta
 r of SBI will introduce the basics and science of biochar\, inc
 luding use of the flame cap kiln\, and demonstrate the integrati
 on of biochar into a compost program.This will be a handson lea
 rning opportunity for agricultural producers of all sizes\, and a
 t the end of the workshop\, attendees will have the resources a
 nd know-how to build a composting program on-site. The workshops
  will be bilingual\, taught in English and Spanish.\n\nLe invitam
 os a participar en el primero de una serie de talleres sobre c
 ompostaje impartidos por Bobby Nicholson\, de Compost Depot\, en 
 colaboración con el Sonoma Ecology Center (SEC) y la Sonoma Bio
 char Initiative (SBI). Estos talleres cuentan con el financiamient
 o de Zero Waste Sonoma (ZWS) y son gratuitos para el público.\
 n\n¡Manos a la obra! El taller ofrecerá pautas prácticas y no
 ciones accesibles de ciencia del suelo para establecer un program
 a de compostaje saludable en el propio lugar de trabajo\, utiliz
 ando recursos disponibles y un modelo escalable. Raymond Baltar\,
  de la SBI\, presentará los fundamentos y la ciencia del bioca
 rbón —incluyendo el uso del horno de tipo "flame cap" kiln—
  y demostrará cómo integrar este material en un programa de c
 ompostaje. \n\nSerá una oportunidad de aprendizaje práctico para
  agricultores\, productores agrícolas\, encargados de jardines o 
 invernaderos y paisajistas de cualquier escala. Al finalizar el t
 aller\, los asistentes contarán con los recursos y los conocimie
 ntos necesarios para implementar un programa de compostaje en sus
  propias instalaciones. Los talleres serán bilingües (impartidos
  en inglés y español).\n\nFecha: Sábado\, 26 de septiembre de
  2026\; de 10:00 a. m. a 1:00 p. m.\n\nLugar: Sonoma Garden Pa
 rk\, 19996 7th St E\, Sonoma\, CA 95476\n\nDirigido a: Agricultor
 es\, productores agrícolas\, encargados de jardines o invernaderos
  y paisajísticas del condado de Sonoma.
LOCATION:Sonoma Garden Park 
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/zero-compost-workshop
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Caribbean Cocktails" Book Release
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T200000
UID:260917mIx5u3sAhkWlHKq8agm3Jg
DESCRIPTION:PREMO Club Presents "Caribbean Cocktails" Book Release \\+ Soc
 ial Mixer\n\nYou are invited to join us for an exclusive experience in the
  heart of Sonoma's wine country to celebrate the upcoming book release "C
 aribbean Cocktails: Drinks & Bites from the Afro-Latino Diaspora"\, \\(Jun
 e 2\, 2026 from Ten Speed Press\\). The book is authored by chef and cockt
 ail creator Nelson German and James Beard Award–winning culinary write
 r Andréa Lawson Gray.\n\nHosted at Aldina Vineyard's Tasting Lounge\,\n
 \nThe evening begins at 5pm with a cocktail \\+ wine reception featuring h
 erbs\, fruits\, and botanicals grown at Little Saint Farm highlighting the
  farm’s seasonal produce. The evening concludes with an author talk.\n\n
 This event is not only a culinary affair\, but also will raise funds for 
 Sprouts Chef Training\, a Bay area-based 501\\(c\\)\\(3\\) nonprofit helpi
 ng under-resourced youth build careers in the culinary industry. Through c
 ulinary training\, mentorship\, and job placement support\, Sprouts equips
  youth to rise from hardship through culinary training and job placement. 
 Graduates use these entry-level jobs to kickstart culinary careers\, pay f
 or education\, or pursue new industries.\n\nVisit https://premoclub.com/e
 vents for more information.
LOCATION:Bacchus Landing
URL:https://premoclub.com/events/caribbean-cocktails-book-release
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ink & Rhythm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T180000
UID:260917iSaoQiCeW0SyydhQ44EvbA
DESCRIPTION:A Live Performance Celebrating Creativity\, Memory & Cultural 
 Connection\n\nExperience an extraordinary collaboration between acclaimed 
 Chinese American artist Jun Jun and internationally celebrated Zimbabwean 
 musician Piwai\, as painting and music unfold together in a live performan
 ce exploring creativity\, memory\, and cultural connection.\n\nThroughout 
 the evening\, Jun Jun will create expressive paintings in real time while 
 Piwai responds through song\, mbira\, and rhythm\, weaving together two ar
 tistic traditions in an improvisational dialogue that transcends language.
  Together\, they invite audiences to experience how art can carry memory\,
  celebrate identity\, and build bridges across cultures.\n\nFollowing the 
 performance\, meet the artists\, explore the exhibition\, and enjoy authen
 tic Zimbabwean cuisine provided by the Zimbabwe Cultural Exchange Project 
 of California.
LOCATION:Petaluma Museum
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/ink-rhythm-tickets-1997155896047?aff=ebds
 oporgprofile
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Memoir Writing Workshop for Women: Crafting Your Life Story
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T130000
