BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Family Garden & Farm Program
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T100000
UID:260915fY1ojHATX0qE9mb5jBsRMA
DESCRIPTION:Vallejo Project is excited to announce the launch of its Fami
 ly Garden & Farm Program\, a hands-on learning experience designed for fam
 ilies with children ages 0–5. The program invites parents and caregivers
  to join young children in exploring gardening\, nature\, healthy food\, a
 nd farm animal experiences at Unity Garden in Vallejo.\n\nThe Family Garde
 n & Farm Program creates opportunities for families to learn and grow toge
 ther through interactive activities that build early childhood development
 \, environmental awareness\, and healthy lifestyle habits.\n\nThrough week
 ly family-centered experiences\, children and caregivers will have the opp
 ortunity to:\n\n Plant flowers\, fruits\, and vegetables  Harvest fresh 
 produce from the garden  Meet and care for friendly farm animals  Feed c
 hickens and goats  Explore nature and outdoor spaces  Learn about health
 y eating and where food comes from  Develop early learning\, communicatio
 n\, and life skills\n\n“Children learn best when they can touch\, explor
 e\, create\, and connect with the world around them\,” said Adjoa McDona
 ld\, Founder of Vallejo Project. “This program brings families together 
 in the garden and farm environment to build confidence\, strengthen relati
 onships\, and create positive memories around food\, nature\, and communit
 y.”\n\nParticipating families will receive hands-on activities\, garden 
 starter resources\, fresh produce opportunities\, and family learning expe
 riences designed to support children’s growth and curiosity.\n\nThe prog
 ram will also measure its impact through family surveys and staff observat
 ions\, tracking outcomes related to:\n\nCaregiver confidence in gardening 
 and teaching children about plants\n\nChildren’s connection to nature an
 d animals\n\nHealthy eating habits\n\nOutdoor learning and exploration\n\n
 Family engagement and community connection\n\nThe Family Garden & Farm Pro
 gram is open to families with children under age five. Space is limited.
LOCATION:Unity Garden
URL:https://www.facebook.com/VallejoProject/posts/pfbid02wHGhL4L19hWTg1jKH
 LYDAZVnqHMdfHLbhsJLCmxHKdDJTCRRGoyNgqfy7Lpxkmwnl
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
