UID:260909YQ8plioMx0egkQDvB3b9XA
DESCRIPTION:Free Admission. Become a member to support Verismo Opera's new
  free admission policy.  Membership for $30 per person will be good for a
  year from purchase and will entitle members to early seating \\(before no
 n-members\\) for performances.\n\n Stage Director: Eliza O’ Malley \n\
 nConductor: Carlos Hernandez\n\nWith Chamber Orchestra and English Supert
 itles \n\nIn association with Mira Theatre Guild\n\nFor company informati
 on and to purchase memberships visit www.verismoopera.org\n\nLove\, lust\
 , jealousy\, deception\, torture\, murder\, suicide – all in one opera 
 – Tosca.  An idealistic artist\, a celebrated singer and a corrupt poli
 ce chief engage in a fierce battle of wills in this tempestuous tale of cr
 uelty and deception. With its themes of political intrigue\, sexual intimi
 dation and official hypocrisy\, Puccini’s great masterpiece rings true t
 oday through its powerfully dramatic and gorgeous music.\n\nMira Theatre G
 uild\, 51 Daniels Avenue\, Vallejo\, CA 94590\n\n- September 12\, 2026 \\(
 Saturday 7:00pm\\)\n\n- September 13           \\(Sunday 3:00pm\
 \)\n\n- September 19           \\(Saturday 7:00pm\\)\n\n- Septem
 ber 20           \\(Sunday 3:00pm\\)\n\n- September 26     
       \\(Saturday 7:00pm\\)\n\n- September 27           \\
 (Sunday 3:00pm\\)
LOCATION:Mira Theatre Guild
URL:http://www.verismoopera.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine\, Women and Dementia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T124500
UID:260909JsuKQy6EU06Aj6zzCP5ZDQ
DESCRIPTION:“Wine\, Women\, & Dementia” is a powerful and uplifting do
 cumentary that will be showcased on Saturday\, September 26\, from 10:00 a
 m -12:45 pm at the Carol Ellis Auditorium at the Santa Rosa Junior College
  Campus\, 680 Sonoma Mountain Parkway\, Petaluma.\n\n The film follows a
  caregiver’s journey across the country\, gathering stories from others 
 navigating dementia care. It captures the beauty and brutality of dementia
  caregiving\, balancing the heartbreaking with the humorous.\n\n Followi
 ng the film\, there will be a panel discussion that includes the filmmaker
 . In addition\, information from local resources will be available.  \n\
 n Please plan to arrive 30–45 minutes early to visit our community reso
 urce tables\, meet representatives from local organizations\, and discover
  services and support available for caregivers and families before the pro
 gram begins.\n\nThis event is sponsored by The Village Network of Petaluma
 \, a nonprofit organization that advocates for innovative community-based
  solutions to improve quality of life and expand choices at all stages of 
 aging.\n\n The event is free of charge\; however\, registration is requir
 ed.  To attend\, contact The Village Network at 707.776.6055
LOCATION:Carol Ellis Auditorium\, Santa Rosa Junior College
URL:https://villagenetworkofpetaluma.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
