BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ART EXHIBIT:  THE DAYS OF VINES AND ROSES
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T180000
UID:260813GtowWVEM7ESawbdPXd0BSw
DESCRIPTION:EPTEMBER ART EXHIBIT:  THE DAYS OF VINES AND ROSES\n\nDate: 
 FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  8/12/26\n\nDATES: August 31 – September 27\, 20
 26\n\nRECEPTION:  SATURDAY\, September 5 – 3 -6 pm Join Donna Schaff
 er and Tosya Shore to celebrate the show and learn about their artistic i
 nspirations.  Refreshments will be served.  \n\nFeatured Artist Donna 
 Schaffer Celebrates Wine Country Beauty in “The Days of Vines and Roses
 ”\n\nSonoma County artist Donna Schaffer unveils her latest collection o
 f oil paintings\, “The Days of Vines and Roses\,” celebrating some of 
 her favorite views of roses blooming among the vineyards\, hills\, and woo
 dlands of Sonoma County. At the heart of the collection is Vines and Trell
 is of Roses\, where glorious pink roses spill across an entrance trellis\,
  set against the orderly rows of a vineyard. In Mini Red Roses Along Viney
 ard\, delicate red roses punctuate the landscape\, creating a lively inter
 play between vineyard rows\, stands of trees\, and the hills beyond. “Li
 ving here in Sonoma County for three decades\, I never tire of its gloriou
 s natural beauty. It is an enduring inspiration and truly a painter’s dr
 eam\,” says Schaffer.\n\nArt has been a focus throughout Schaffer’s li
 fe. She has been painting full time in Dry Creek since the mid-1990s and i
 s particularly known for her paintings of Sonoma County’s wine country. 
 Her work are popular with both locals and visitors who want to bring a bit
  of Sonoma’s beauty and magic into their own homes. Schaffer has been a 
 member of the Upstairs Art Gallery for more than 25 years and has exhibite
 d regionally\, including eight years as an Art Trails artist.\n\nMeet the 
 artist:  Schaffer will be hosting the Gallery on September 3 and 27 from
  11-6 pm.  \n\nStairway Showcase: Tosya Shore — “It’s Black and Wh
 ite with a Splash of Color”\n\nThe Stairway Showcase presents artist Tos
 ya Shore’s “It’s Black and White with a Splash of Color\,” a colle
 ction of watercolors that begins with the fundamentals of composition: red
 ucing an image to its two most essential elements—black and white. Worki
 ng with ink\, a stick\, and a scraper\, Shore roughens the edges of her su
 bjects and strips away unnecessary detail\, allowing light itself—not fo
 rm or precision—to take center stage. Her paintings invite the viewer to
  experience the essence of a scene through contrast\, gesture\, and the ex
 pressive qualities of the medium.\n\nIn addition to her watercolor works\,
  Shore presents paintings inspired by a recent trip to Carmel\, where she 
 picked up oil paint for the first time and explored painting the ocean usi
 ng nothing but a palette knife. The resulting works introduce a vibrant sp
 lash of color and texture into a practice grounded in restraint—new pigm
 ent\, new surface\, yet the same enduring fascination with light over like
 ness.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Indian Museum and Cultural Center 30th Anniversary Gala
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T210000
UID:260812kaL2N0UImUC2ZOywMtmrgA
DESCRIPTION:For 30 years\, the California Indian Museum and Cultural Cente
 r \\(CIMCC\\) has been a vital and unique resource advancing understanding
  of California Indian history\, cultures\, and contemporary leadership. On
  Saturday\, September 26\, 2026\, at 5:00 pm\, CIMCC will celebrate three 
 decades of impact with an anniversary gala —an inspiring evening honorin
 g Indigenous excellence\, celebrating community\, and looking toward the n
 ext generation of Native leadership.\n\nThe event will showcase the richne
 ss\, resilience\, and creativity of Native communities while raising criti
 cal funds to advance CIMCC’s work to preserve and share cultural knowled
 ge\, strengthen intergenerational connections\, empower Native youth and f
 amilies\, and nurture Indigenous leadership for generations to come.\n\nGu
 ests will be treated to an unforgettable Native traditional food dinner pr
 epared by award-winning Chef Justin Pioche\, a 2023 James Beard Award Fina
 list for Best Chef of the Southwest \\(AZ\, NM\, NV\, OK\\) and Food Netwo
 rk Chopped Champion. The evening will also feature a cocktail reception\, 
 silent auction\, inspiring stories of CIMCC’s impact\, and vibrant Nativ
 e entertainment—all set against the beautiful backdrop of Balletto Viney
 ards in Santa Rosa.
LOCATION:Balletto Vineyards
URL:https://cimcc.org/gala/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JP's Backyard Ultra/Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T180000
UID:260812QK01QtkC5kGc-IGCekMGKg
DESCRIPTION:Event Description\n\nJoin us for JP’s Backyard Ultra\, a one
 -of-a-kind ultramarathon and hike set in the scenic trails of Skyline Wild
 erness Park in Napa\, CA. Now in its fourth and final year\, this grassroo
 ts event is more than just a race\, it’s a celebration of life\, resilie
 nce\, and community.\n\nBorn from my personal journey with Stage IV medias
 tinal paraganglioma\, JP’s Backyard Ultra is a fundraiser for the Pheo P
 ara Alliance\, a 501\\(c\\)\\(3\\) nonprofit \\(EIN 26-1510652\\) dedicate
 d to empowering patients\, families\, and medical professionals affected b
 y pheochromocytoma and paraganglioma through education\, advocacy\, and gl
 obal support. Learn more at www.pheopara.org.\n\nWhether you’re in it fo
 r one loop or ten\, come run or hike in solidarity\, to honor those facing
  rare diseases\, to challenge yourself\, and to stand as part of a growing
  force for good.\n\n~Jonathan Pascual\n\nThe course features a 3.3 mile lo
 op with 550\\+ feet of climbing\, offering a mix of terrain from steep roc
 ky sections to shaded paths. Scroll down for map below.\n\nParticipants ca
 n choose anywhere from 1 to 10 loops.\n\nRunners and hikers alike start at
  the same time every hour going clockwise on the even hours and counterclo
 ckwise on the odd hours. So it doesn’t matter if you finish your loop fa
 st or slow because everyone starts again at the same time in the next hour
 . Those attempting 10 loops should pace themselves for a final race on the
  10th loop making 33.3 miles. You can do as many or as few loops as you wi
 sh however.\n\nTimed Event: 8:00 AM – 6:00 PM. Please arrive by 0730 for
  course description\, announcement of run prize categories & fundraising p
 rizes.\n\nAid Station: Main camp has various caloric options and drinks wi
 th water only at the bridge and mile 2.3.\n\nFood & Beverages: Provided\, 
 including lunch for participants and volunteers.\n\nCupless Event: Bring y
 our own water bottle or hydration pack. HYDRAPAK\, our Sustainable Racing 
 Partner will provide limited 300 Limited Edition HydraPak Graphic SpeedCup
 s & 8 SpeedFill Pitchers for use at aid stations.\n\nAwards:Medals to all 
 registered hikers and runners.Medal & wine \\(non-alcoholic option for und
 er 21\\) for top three male and female finishers of the 2\, 4\, 6\, 8 loop
 s.Medal\, wine\, and trophy for the fastest 10th loop goes to the top thre
 e male and female finishers and special Vinerunner 4th place trophy.Medal\
 , wine\, and trophy for the fastest cumulative time for 10 loops goes to t
 he top three male and female finishers.\n\nRaffle Prizes: buy tickets on d
 ay of event to win raffle baskets\, gift certificates\, and other special 
 prizes. Proceeds benefit the Pheo Para Alliance.\n\nSilent Wine Auction: p
 lace your bids on exceptional wines generously donated by local Napa Valle
 y wineries\, starting at an unbeatable buy-now price. Proceeds benefit the
  Pheo Para Alliance.\n\nRegistration “Fee”: Donation LinkJP’s Backya
 rd Ultra has always been a free event. Suggested donation to register star
 ts at $30.Participants get a medal\, a variety of snacks and drinks at the
  aid station\, and lunch.To streamline registration\, we are using runsign
 up.com. 100% of suggested starting donation of $30 goes directly to the Ph
 eo Para Alliance. The processing fee of 6% per $1 of transaction \\(cart\\
 ). This fee is charged per transaction\, not per individual participant\, 
 meaning that if a user registers multiple people to a single cart\, the $1
  fee is only charged once\, lowering the overall cost per person.If you ca
 nnot attend or want to donate beyond the suggested amount\, consider givin
 g an additional donation at the donation link.\n\nParking:Do not park at S
 kyline’s main parking lot to avoid parking fee. Parking opens at 0600.Fo
 llow signs for “JP’s Backyard Ultra Parking” for free parking for re
 gistered participants at the Westside parking lot of Skyline Wilderness Pa
 rk.\n\nChildcare: We have volunteers to watch your kids from 0800-1200.\n\
 nPark Rules: No dogs on trails\, stay on marked trails\, carry out your tr
 ash & put in appropriate bins at the main aid station\, trails close at su
 nset.\n\nCamp with us: reservations at Skyline’s Website: Reserve Camp S
 ite. Mention JP’s Backyard Ultra to reserve your spot in our campsite on
  Friday 9/25 & Saturday 9/26. Camping reservation with vehicles is nearby 
 but will be separate from the tent only camping.
LOCATION:Skyline Wilderness Park
URL:https://pheopara.org/jps-backyard-ultra-hike-sept-26-2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sullivan Rutherford Estate's Annual Event of Artistry & Excellence
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T180000
UID:260812OtRljeQh3kGYNJII_L_BYA
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Saturday\, September 26th from 3:00 p.m. to 6:00 p.
 m. for an afternoon celebrating excellence\, creativity\, and authenticity
  at the intersection of wine\, art\, and hospitality at Sullivan Rutherfor
 d Estate.\n\nSet against the backdrop of harvest in Rutherford\, Napa Vall
 ey\, guests will gather around a grand table for a thoughtfully curated ex
 perience featuring exceptional wines from Sullivan Rutherford Estate Winem
 aker Jeff Cole\, extraordinarily inventive cuisine from one of the Napa Va
 lley’s most renowned chefs and meaningful conversation. James Beard Awar
 d-winning Chef Rogelio Garcia will present a four-course culinary journey 
 inspired by the season's finest ingredients\, thoughtfully crafted in dial
 ogue with the artistic expressions of both ceramicist Adán Paredes and Wi
 nemaker Jeff Cole. Live music will provide the soundtrack to an afternoon 
 designed to foster connection\, celebrate creativity and a shared apprecia
 tion for craftsmanship\, artistry\, and excellence.\n\nThroughout the even
 t\, guests will have the opportunity to engage with world-renowned ceramic
  artist Adán Paredes\, whose work reflects a lifelong dedication to craft
 smanship and creative expression. Joining him will be Sullivan Rutherford 
 Estate’s Winemaker Jeff Cole\, whose own artistry takes shape in the vin
 eyard and cellar in order to produce the most iconic Merlot and Cabernet S
 auvignon expressions of Rutherford. Throughout the afternoon\, guests will
  enjoy a curated selection of wines\, including a limited preview of an un
 released bottling of our Family Reserve available exclusively for this cel
 ebration.\n\nHarvest is a season that reminds us that the most meaningful 
 experiences are rarely created alone. They emerge through patience\, colla
 boration\, dedication\, perseverance and a shared commitment to excellence
 . This celebration brings together three distinct forms of artistry: winem
 aking\, creative cuisine\, and one-of-a-kind visual expressions for an unf
 orgettable afternoon among friends. Tickets are $425 per guest\, or $550 f
 or two tickets for Founder’s Members.
LOCATION:Sullivan Rutherford Estate
URL:https://sullivanwine.com/harvest-party/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Boathouse Wine & Food Pairing Experience – Cuvaison and Bran
 dlin Estate
