BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tim Kliphuis & Jimmy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T190000
UID:260910K7ZOKxQlF0SH0J4T2kh_DQ
DESCRIPTION:Native to Northern California\, Jimmy Grant  grew up in a hous
 ehold full of rich musical influences. While his early  influences also in
 cluded Russian Folk\, Balkan\, traditional Hungarian\,  Bluegrass\, Celtic
  and Classical\,  from a young age he gravitated towards the music of Djan
 go Reinhardt.  He plays a blend of musics from all over the world and his 
 own compositions.    He has studied with  acclaimed guitarists Jim Nichols
  and Howard Alden\, and in addition to  Django Reinhardt\, his other major
  musical influences are Bach\, Kovacs  Andor\, Roby Lakatos and Angelo Deb
 arre. He has performed  with artists such as David Grisman\, Paulus Schaef
 er \,Tim Kliphuis\,  Gonzalo Bergara\, Ludovic Beier\, Velvet Caravan\, Rh
 ythm Future Quartet\,  Hot Club of San Francisco and more\, and has played
  at the Savannah Musci  Festival\, Los Angeles Django Reinhardt Festival\,
   Nor-Cal Jazz Fest\, Djangofest Northwest and The New York Hot Jazz  Fest
 ival.    He has recorded two albums under his own name\, and performed on 
 several other albums. Jimmy's original song “Insomnia” was a finalist 
 in the John Lennon songwriting competition\\(in the jazz category\\). As J
 immy puts  it\, “We believe that Jazz\, and the music of Django\, is a p
 iece of history worth preserving.” \n\n In addition to performing\, Jimm
 y teaches private  students and has been on the faculty of the Django in J
 une Festival in  Massachusetts\, and also is the artistic director of the 
 Django Reinhardt  Association.  Jimmy also writes for “Gypsy Jazz Secret
 s Magazine”.   He has been featured in Relix magazine and Acoustic Guita
 r magazine.
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108725663?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Henry Frank: J-80928: A Human Experience Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T170000
UID:2609062boa-uDL9kSDN64btJ8DaA
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center is proud to present f
 eatured September artist **Henry Frank** in the Del Mue Galleries this Se
 ptember. There will be a reception for the artist as part of the Internati
 onal Day of Peace Festival Finale on **September 20 from 2 – 6 pm**.\n\n
 **J-80928: A Human Experience Exhibition** explores Henry Frank’s trans
 formative journey through nearly three decades of incarceration in the Cal
 ifornia Department of Corrections. Through deeply personal artwork\, the e
 xhibition reflects on trauma\, friendship\, identity\, hope\, and personal
  growth while inviting viewers to recognize the humanity and capacity for 
 change in people who are incarcerated.\n\n**ARTISTS STATEMENT** **J-80928:
  A Human Experience Exhibition** explores my personal journey serving a 29
 -year-to-life sentence in the California Department of Corrections as an I
 ndigenous person\, an artist\, and a human being. I was incarcerated from 
 February 15\, 1994\, to April 19\, 2013\, and during much of that time\, I
  lived hour to hour. For the first 14 years\, my mantras were: expect the 
 worst and hope for the best\, trust no one except myself\, and fear is a s
 tate of mind. While many experiences were deeply traumatic\, there were al
 so moments of humanity\, compassion\, joy\, and empathy that transformed h
 ow I saw myself and the world around me.\n\nThe last six years of my incar
 ceration became the most transformative period of my life. I began to beli
 eve that I would not die in prison. I found hope\, discovered the importan
 ce of serving others\, began to see myself as a serious artist\, and gain
 ed a deeper understanding of my place in the world. My mantras evolved int
 o: expect the best and be prepared for anything less\, trust everyone unti
 l they give me a reason not to\, and happiness is a choice. During this ti
 me\, I learned to love and respect myself\, to be accountable\, to live in
  the present\, to be a true friend\, and to serve others with intention an
 d compassion.\n\nThis exhibition is an oeuvre dedicated to the experiences
 \, emotional trauma\, friendships\, and reclamation of identity that shape
 d me throughout my incarceration. Through this body of work\, I hope peopl
 e can connect with parts of my journey and recognize that I am not so diff
 erent from them. More importantly\, I want to humanize those who are curre
 ntly incarcerated and raise awareness that people are capable of change. T
 hey can become contributing members of their communities. They have famili
 es\, hobbies\, hopes\, dreams\, and the capacity for growth and transforma
 tion.\n\nI have been working toward completing this body of work and plan 
 to have the exhibition finished completely by the end of this year.\n\nThi
 s exhibition is partially funded by an Artist Fellowship Grant from the Ar
 t for Justice Fund. I am grateful for their support and patience for this 
 exhibition to evolve into its fullest potential.\n\nHuman Being\n\nHenry E
 dward Frank\n\nYurok and Kashaya Pomo
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/henry-fr
 ank-j-80928-a-human-experience-exhibition
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Golden Hour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T170000
UID:260903di8jt_qDzEOwHCxGvr8qgA
DESCRIPTION:This September and October\, Lucci Lambrusco is taking over 
 Golden Hour at El Dorado Kitchen\, bringing a taste of Italian aperitivo
  culture to the patio all season long.\n\nSettle in for a late afternoon o
 f Lucci Lambrusco\, Italian wines\, cocktails and shareable bites made for
  lingering. Throughout the two-month takeover\, Lucci will be joined every
  Thursday by a rotating lineup of guest wineries\, importers and producers
 \, each stopping by to pour something special and share a little more abou
 t what’s in your glass.\n\nThe season kicks off on Thursday\, September
  3\, with live music\, Lucci Lambrusco\, passed pizzas and arancini on the
  patio.\n\nLUCCI ITALIAN GOLDEN HOUR TAKEOVER Monday–Friday | 3:00–
 5:00 PM September & October\n\nTHURSDAY GUEST WINE SERIES Every Thursday |
  3:00–5:00 PM\n\nSeptember 3 | Lucci Lambrusco\n\nSeptember 10 | Oliver 
 McCrum Wines\n\nSeptember 17 | Mora Estate\n\nSeptember 24 | Idlewild Wine
 s\n\nOctober 1 | Cline Family Cellars\n\nOctober 8 | Unti Vineyards\n\nOct
 ober 15 | Massican\n\n...and more to come!\n\nLucci is pouring all season 
 long\, with a few friends joining along the way.\n\nCome for a glass. Stay
  for another.\n\nJOIN US FOR GOLDEN HOUR
LOCATION:El Dorado Hotel
URL:https://eldoradosonoma.com/el-dorado-kitchen/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
