DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260930T170000
UID:260903Od9IbNxsRkm0oSyu1zEknw
DESCRIPTION:This September and October\, Lucci Lambrusco is taking over 
 Golden Hour at El Dorado Kitchen\, bringing a taste of Italian aperitivo
  culture to the patio all season long.\n\nSettle in for a late afternoon o
 f Lucci Lambrusco\, Italian wines\, cocktails and shareable bites made for
  lingering. Throughout the two-month takeover\, Lucci will be joined every
  Thursday by a rotating lineup of guest wineries\, importers and producers
 \, each stopping by to pour something special and share a little more abou
 t what’s in your glass.\n\nThe season kicks off on Thursday\, September
  3\, with live music\, Lucci Lambrusco\, passed pizzas and arancini on the
  patio.\n\nLUCCI ITALIAN GOLDEN HOUR TAKEOVER Monday–Friday | 3:00–
 5:00 PM September & October\n\nTHURSDAY GUEST WINE SERIES Every Thursday |
  3:00–5:00 PM\n\nSeptember 3 | Lucci Lambrusco\n\nSeptember 10 | Oliver 
 McCrum Wines\n\nSeptember 17 | Mora Estate\n\nSeptember 24 | Idlewild Wine
 s\n\nOctober 1 | Cline Family Cellars\n\nOctober 8 | Unti Vineyards\n\nOct
 ober 15 | Massican\n\n...and more to come!\n\nLucci is pouring all season 
 long\, with a few friends joining along the way.\n\nCome for a glass. Stay
  for another.\n\nJOIN US FOR GOLDEN HOUR
LOCATION:El Dorado Hotel
URL:https://eldoradosonoma.com/el-dorado-kitchen/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kendra Scott "Born to Shine" Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260930T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260930T203000
UID:260823QpPKo_6G5ka3S6ycnijOlg
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the new Kendra Scott store in Montgomery Village fo
 r a two-part book club experience! Throughout the month\, we’ll read Ken
 dra Scott’s Born To Shine together while building community and creating
  deeper connection with women across Sonoma County.\n\nAttire: Come wearin
 g whatever makes you feel confident and comfortable. Stretchy pants & tenn
 is shoes are always acceptable at She Can Club!\n\nPart 1: Wednesday 8/26 
 6:30 – 8:30pm: Book Club Kickoff\n\nPick up your hardcover copy of Born 
 to Shine and meet your fellow book club members. We’ll spend the evening
  getting to know one another\, sharing what brought us to the book club\, 
 and launching our Instagram group chat so we can stay connected and encour
 age each other between events.\n\nPart 2: Wednesday 9/30\, 6:30–8:30pm: 
 Bedazzle & Reflect\n\nReunite with the group for a fun and creative book c
 over bedazzling party. As we craft\, we’ll explore the reflection questi
 ons from the back of the book\, voluntarily share our biggest takeaways\, 
 celebrate one another’s growth\, and deepen the connections we’ve buil
 t throughout the month.\n\nBoth events include:\n\n• A non-alcoholic Sip
  & Shop and Color Bar® experience\n\n• Light bites and non-alcoholic re
 freshments\n\n• Access to the Instagram group chat\n\n• All bedazzling
  supplies\n\n• A hardcover copy of Born to Shine \\($28 value\\)\n\nAs a
 n added bonus\, Kendra Scott will donate 20% of event sales to She Can Clu
 b to further support women in Sonoma County.\n\nThe $40 ticket price inclu
 des access to both events. Due to the nature of the experience and include
 d materials\, tickets cannot be discounted for attendees who are only able
  to attend one event.\n\nSorry\, no refunds as spots are limited at this e
 vent.\n\nIf you have any questions\, please email Hilary at heyhilary@shec
 anclub.com or DM her on Instagram @shecanclub.
LOCATION:Kendra Scott in Montgomery Village
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/kendra-scott-born-to-shine-book-
 club/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
