BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Home Again\, Home Again
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T200000
UID:260926n4lLFGLUa0mInk-pwqOMiQ
DESCRIPTION:On View\n\nOctober 1 – November 1\, 2026 9 AM – 8 PM · 7 
 Days a Week\n\nOpening Reception\n\nThu\, October 1 · 5 – 7:30 PM First
  Thursday Sonoma Art Walk\n\nwhere\n\nGallery 212 276 E. Napa St.\, Sonoma
 \n\nadmission\n\nFree Open to the public 9 AM – 8 PM\n\nArtist Statement
 :\n\nHome is the place we return to\, the place we care for\, the place we
  imagine will sustain us. But what happens when the place we call home bec
 omes increasingly overwhelmed by the things we have made and discarded?\n\
 nSince 1999\, we have collected plastic from Kehoe Beach in the Point Reye
 s National Seashore\, bringing home what the ocean has returned to us. Wha
 t began as an encounter with plastic pollution has become something much l
 arger: an ongoing meditation on our relationship with the planet and on th
 e extraordinary persistence of the materials we create.\n\nPlastic is now 
 woven into nearly every aspect of contemporary life. It surrounds us\, car
 ries our food\, packages our purchases\, clothes our bodies\, and fills ou
 r homes. Once discarded\, however\, it rarely disappears. It fragments\, t
 ravels\, accumulates\, and finds its way into rivers\, oceans\, soil\, air
 \, and the bodies of living things. The shoreline becomes a kind of ledger
 —a record of our habits and our collective failure to imagine where our 
 things go when we are finished with them.\n\nOur work is an effort at plan
 etary housekeeping: picking up\, sorting\, washing\, arranging\, and trans
 forming what has been left behind. There is something humble and almost do
 mestic about this work. We gather the fragments as one might sweep a floor
  or tidy a room\, except that the room is the world itself.\n\nThe title H
 ome Again\, Home Again carries a double meaning. It speaks to the desire t
 o return to a place that feels familiar and cared for\, while reminding us
  that there is no separate place to return to. This is our home. The ocean
 \, the shoreline\, the rivers\, and the landscapes around us are not somew
 here else—they are part of the same household.\n\nBy transforming discar
 ded plastic into art\, we are not trying to make pollution beautiful or to
  disguise the problem. Rather\, we want to hold these objects in our atten
 tion long enough to see them differently: as evidence of our choices\, as 
 traces of daily life\, and as reminders of our profound dependence on the 
 natural world.\n\nPerhaps planetary housekeeping begins with simply paying
  attention—seeing what has accumulated\, picking it up\, and asking what
  kind of home we want to leave behind.\n\n*Richard Lang and Judith Selby L
 ang One Beach Plastic*
LOCATION:Gallery 212
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/home-again-home-again/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Thursday Nights with DJ BRXNDO – Live in The Lounge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T235900
UID:260924vCaWOC6h40iHFEOmJHJyzQ
DESCRIPTION:THURSDAY NIGHTS WITH DJ BRXNDO OPEN FORMAT • REQUESTS • DA
 NCING • NO COVER\n\nThursday nights have a new home in The Lounge at Bar
 rel Proof. Every Thursday at 9 PM\, DJ BRXNDO takes over the front room wi
 th an open-format set built around the crowd\, the dance floor and your re
 quests.\n\nBRXNDO has been making his way through the Bay Area nightlife s
 cene\, spinning parties from Santa Rosa to San Francisco. Now he's settlin
 g into a weekly Thursday night residency at Barrel Proof.\n\nOpen format m
 eans just that: no single genre gets to run the night. BRXNDO can move thr
 ough Reggaeton\, Hip-Hop\, Latin hits\, Top 40\, throwbacks\, dance tracks
  and party favorites depending on where the room takes him.\n\nHear someth
 ing you want? Make a request.\n\nSome Thursdays might lean Latin. Some mig
 ht turn into a throwback party. Some nights might go somewhere completely 
 different. BRXNDO reads the room and keeps it moving.\n\nWhatever else is 
 happening at Barrel Proof that night\, The Lounge belongs to BRXNDO every 
 Thursday at 9.\n\nDJ BRXNDO Every Thursday 9 PM The Lounge at Barrel Proof
  501 Mendocino Ave • Downtown Santa Rosa 21+ No Cover\n\nCheck out **www
 .BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/thursday-nights-with-dj-brxndo-live-in-th
 e-lounge-tickets-2002239002756?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
