BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening with Wolf Run
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T223000
UID:260916QgP0iKk8YkCSbsMfYi8Yww
DESCRIPTION:**Wolf Run** The beginnings of Wolf Run germinated in 2010 wh
 en Adam Traum and Jack Hines met at an open mic in Sonoma\, California. Th
 e two started chatting\, and got together shortly after that to jam on a r
 ainy winter afternoon in a cabin in Glen Ellen. Traum got home and told hi
 s wife\, "I think I found my bassist!"\n\nAs they began playing local gigs
 \, and later traveling to out-of-town shows\, their bond grew and cemented
  their friendship. The duo needed a name and liked the idea of "Wolf Run\,
 " a neighborhood near Hines' house\, not far from Jack London State Park.\
 n\nThe mostly original music they play makes it difficult to put Wolf Run 
 in a box. They fluidly move between songs in a wide range of genres that i
 nclude Americana\, blues\, folk\, country and rock while still sounding co
 hesive. Adam Traum is a prolific songwriter\, often enlisting the help of 
 Hines to bring a song home. Hines brings some terrific songs to the band a
 s well.\n\nSubbing for veteran drummer Kendrick Freeman\, is another pro\,
  Gabe Ford\, who has toured with Little Feat and many other bands. The ban
 d plays songs ranging from acoustic singer-songwriter feels\, to funky gro
 oves\, and full-tilt rock and roll.\n\nhttps://www.wolfrun.net\n\nhttps://
 www.facebook.com/WolfRun707/\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/adam\\_traum/
LOCATION:The Lost Church Santa Rosa
URL:https://thelostchurch.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket#/instances/a0FUh0
 00009FAZlMAO
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
