BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SCRIBE at Shady Oak Barrel House
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T220000
UID:260912bdbrCgIhP0CLQAaHYvd4qg
DESCRIPTION:SCRIBE: Alternative progressive rock with an indie heart. \n\
 nScribe is bringing emotionally charged power-trio rock that blends intric
 ate musicianship with accessible songwriting.  Musical skill\, and acrob
 atic\, yet accessible rock songwriting come together into a sleek and raw 
 power trio!  \n\nThere is something slightly unfashionable about a great
  power trio. No studio excess to hide behind\, no sprawling cast of musici
 ans to dilute the chemistry. Just bass\, guitar\, drums and three players 
 who have to make every note count.  Northern California’s SCRIBE under
 stands the challenge\, but they also seem to relish it.  Influences rang
 e from Rush\, to The Police\, Pink Floyd\, Led Zeppelin\, The Doors\, **M
 usicals\, Jam Bands\, R&B\, Jazz\, Folk\, and Classical music. The result 
 is a sophisticated\, yet approachable sound\, balancing technical precisio
 n with raw emotion and memorable hooks.**
LOCATION:Shady Oak Barrel House
URL:https://scriberocks.com/event/6712229/777494293/scribe-shady-oak-barre
 l-house
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Start With What & Why: A Procrastinator's Guide to Stop Overthinki
 ng
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T110000
UID:260912RipYr4M4YEipdKJBZM8Vvg
DESCRIPTION:Start With What & Why: A Procrastinator's Guide to Stop Overth
 inking\n\nFeeling stuck in the endless loop of overthinking and procrastin
 ation?\n\nYou’ve accomplished a lot. So why does it feel like something 
 is still missing?\n\nIt’s taken me decades to get honest about what I re
 ally wanted to do with the rest of my life. It doesn’t have to take you 
 that long.\n\nIf you’re an ambitious overthinker\, tired of knowing what
  to do and still not doing it\, this session is built for you.\n\nIn one h
 our\, we’ll work through three things together\, live:\n\n• Why you fe
 el stuck \\(and why you’re not broken\\)\n\n• What you actually want\,
  and why it matters to you\n\n• One real next step\, named and written d
 own before you leave\n\nNo fluff. No 20-step system. Just honest\, practic
 al work you can use the same day.\n\nI am A Guide You Can Trust\n\nI’ve 
 been in the trenches of personal growth\, recovery\, and business for deca
 des. I understand what it feels like to be at rock bottom\, and I also kno
 w the sweetness of victory.\n\nThe greatest and most lasting victories in 
 my life are the internal ones. The shifts that rewired how I think\, belie
 ve\, and act. The habits I resisted kicking and screaming\, and finally ha
 d no other choice but to let go of if I wanted to grow.\n\nSome call them 
 bad habits. Some call them sins. I call them human.\n\nThis is how I coach
 . This is what I teach. And it comes from a place of care\, because I’ve
  been there.\n\n35 Years In. Still Doing the Work.\n\n• 35\\+ years in s
 ales and marketing\, 80%\\+ client retention rate\n\n• 40\\+ years of so
 briety and personal recovery\n\n• 7 books written and published\n\n• A
 wards from the New York Times / RMG: Salesperson and Employee of the Year\
 n\n• Past President\, Toastmasters of Petaluma · Past President\, Redwo
 od Writers\n\n• 2025 Recipient\, Jack London Award for Service to Redwoo
 d Writers\n\n• Certified NLP Practitioner & Life Coach\n\nResults and ac
 colades don’t tell the whole story. The real credential is this: I’m s
 till doing the work. Still growing. Still getting humbled. Still showing u
 p.\n\nThis Might be for You if:\n\n• You’re successful on the outside 
 and quietly restless on the inside\n\n• You’re tired of knowing what t
 o do and still not doing it\n\n• You’re leading others while secretly 
 running empty\n\n• You’re done with surface-level advice that doesn’
 t stick\n\n• You’re ready to stop going it alone\n\nYou already know w
 hat to do. You simply have to be bold enough to become willing to take you
 r first step forward.\n\nIf you’re ready\, don't wait\, register today.
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/start-with-what-why-a-procrastinators-gui
 de-to-stop-overthinking-tickets-1999513816651
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dear Evan Hansen
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T163000
UID:260911iy-nZlAw4kqj0tam9XtWKg
DESCRIPTION:Poignant\, raw\, and of-the-moment\, Dear Evan Hansen pulls ba
 ck the curtain on the profound desire for human connection in the digital 
 age\, offering an empathetic look at the alienation of young people naviga
 ting modern social pressures.\n\nThe story follows Evan\, a high school se
 nior struggling with severe social anxiety who writes motivational letters
  to himself as a therapeutic exercise. When a troubled classmate dies by s
 uicide with one of Evan’s letters in his pocket\, the boy's grieving par
 ents mistakenly believe Evan was his secret best friend. Desperate to comf
 ort them\, Evan plays along\, spiraling into a web of fabricated emails an
 d internet fame before he must ultimately face the truth.\n\nPowered by a 
 critically acclaimed pop-rock score and the sweeping anthems\, Dear Even H
 ansen is a powerful reminder that we are never truly alone. Spreckels is p
 roud to present the North Bay premiere of this six-time Tony Award winning
  musical!
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/dear-evan-hansen/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Apple U-Pick at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T113000
UID:260911ORgk4H6vtU60S8wKPmEJFw
DESCRIPTION:**Our popular Apple U-Pick Experiences return for a second yea
 r!**\n\nExperience the magic of harvest season at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
 \, where you can hand-select the most flavorful Honeycrisp or Fuji apples 
 straight from our certified organic orchard.\n\nTimed entries from 8:30am.
  Last orchard entry at 11:30am.\n\nAdmission: $8 for adults\, $3 for child
 ren. Registration required.\n\nU-Pick apples: $4 per pound.\n\n**Apple U-P
 ick FAQs** \n\nDo I need a reservation? \n\nYes! Please reserve your tim
 e slot on our reservation site. Reservations help us ensure everyone has a
  wonderful experience without overcrowding.  \n\nCan I show up without a
  reservation? \n\nWe require reservations to maintain our capacity limit
 s and ensure everyone enjoys their visit to the fullest.  \n\nCan I canc
 el my reservation?  \n\nAbsolutely! You can cancel your reservation up 
 to 48 hours before your scheduled time by calling us at 707-823-3100. Plea
 se note that cancellations made less than 48 hours in advance will result 
 in forfeiture of the entrance fee. \n\nCan I bring my dog?  \n\nDogs a
 re not permitted in the orchard\, with the exception of service animals. T
 his policy helps ensure the safety and comfort of all our visitors. \n\nC
 an I bring a stroller into the orchard?  \n\nFor safety reasons\, strol
 lers aren't allowed in the orchard\, but you're welcome to leave yours at 
 the check-in area where it will be safe and waiting for you!  \n\nI requ
 ire mobility accommodations. Can I still pick apples in the orchard?  \n
 \nYes. Please call us on 707-823-3110 once you’re made a reservation and
  we can provide suitable transportation into our orchard.\n\nWhy is there 
 an entrance fee?  \n\nThe entrance fee helps us maintain our beautiful 
 orchard and keep our experienced staff on hand to ensure everyone has a sa
 fe and enjoyable experience. \n\nHow much are the apples?  \n\nOur del
 icious U-pick apples are $4.00 per pound.  \n\nWhat variety of apples wi
 ll we be harvesting?  \n\nYou'll be picking either Honeycrisp or Fuji a
 pples (depending on seasonal availability).  \n\nCan I harvest heirloom 
 apples?  \n\nWhile heirloom apples aren't available for U-pick\, we off
 er many wonderful heirloom varieties for purchase in our Farm Shop.  \n\
 nAre your apples organic?  \n\nYes\, all our apples are organically gro
 wn and certified annually by Oregon Tilth!
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://goldridgeorganicfarms.ticketspice.com/u-pick
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lou Hazel
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T200000
UID:260910jHE4BVf1I0m44p7c9BUCzg
DESCRIPTION:Lou Hazel was born in the town of Olean\, New York to a family
  of northeastern wiseacres.\n\nNot one to commit\, he skirted the compulsi
 ve hunting and fishing tradition held close to his father’s heart - inst
 ead cultivating a sensitivity more suited to artists and vagabonds. As a r
 esult\, his travels brought him across the country and eventually through 
 debilitating depression before coming to rest with a sense of personal pea
 ce and positivity in Durham\, NC.\n\nYet\, Lou’s brain is still a bat ca
 ve. Mostly\, he wakes up with no idea what he’s going to do next\, then 
 finds himself there. In songwriting\, he pulls from this cave rambling\, h
 eartfelt tales flowing through unselfconscious truth. In illustrations\, h
 e swirls and meanders towards an eventual finish only understood upon comp
 letion – as in his music. And in his photography and design work\, he re
 nders the essence of fellow musicians into expressive\, personalized works
  of art.\n\nToday\, Louie continues crafting genuine folk tales of honest 
 longing\, disquieting loss\, and nostalgia through a brilliant sheen of fr
 esh insight with humble humor. Grabbing us by the ears in a new-age\, Prin
 e-like grip. Transforming the minutiae of everyday life into ever more evo
 cative music. And surprising us all\, including himself\, with where we em
 erge.\n\nIn other words\, Lou Hazel is coming out of this unbearable\, unb
 elievably tragic\, disconcerting year like a damn newborn moth with jet en
 gine wings aimed toward a totally full super-moon. And it is good.
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108769759?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Geology of Laguna de Santa Rosa (Part 2 of the Triple Watershe
 d Series)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T130000
UID:260910Yu2X73qx70SRcSDSo6n84w
DESCRIPTION:Join geologist Nicole Myers\, CEI's Program and Outreach Speci
 alist\, to explore the geologic history of the three watersheds of Sonoma 
 Mountain. Learn how the formation of the San Andreas Fault System lifted t
 he rocks of Sonoma Mountain out of the depths of the ocean\, then caused m
 illions of years of volcanic eruptions. Explore the oceanic and volcanic r
 ocks of the mountain that record 180 million years of Earth history\, the 
 faults that have formed beautiful landscapes over the last 20 million year
 s\, and the streams that have been carved into the mountain as water flows
  to the Pacific Ocean by way of the Russian River and San Pablo Bay. \\*Th
 is event is part of a series! Check out the Petaluma River Watershed event
  at Lafferty Ranch on September 19th at 9-11:30am\, a collaboration with S
 onoma Mountain Preservation & Landpaths. The Sonoma Creek Watershed Rockto
 ber event at Jack London State Historic Park is on October 17th at 11am-3p
 m in a collaboration with Jack London Park Partners\\*
LOCATION:Fairfield Osborn Preserve
URL:https://cei.sonoma.edu/triple-watershed-series-laguna-de-santa-rosa
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bye Bye Birdie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T213000
UID:260910SLJeyUj-xUeoC9QBNLLKJg
DESCRIPTION:A joyful\, high-energy musical comedy packed with unforgettabl
 e songs\, humor\, and heart\, "Bye Bye Birdie" is a celebration of youth\,
  fame\, and the delightful chaos that happens when pop culture collides wi
 th small-town life.\n\nFrom the high-energy “The Telephone Hour” to th
 e show-stopping “A Lot of Livin’ to Do\,” the heartfelt “How Lovel
 y to Be a Woman\,” and the iconic “Put On a Happy Face\,” this produ
 ction is filled with classic musical theater moments the whole family can 
 enjoy.\n\nCinnabar Theater's production is directed by Zachary Hasbany\, w
 ith book by Michael Stewart\, music by Charles Strouse\, and lyrics by Lee
  Adams\, originally produced by Edward Padula. The show is presented throu
 gh special arrangement with Concord Theatricals.\n\nShow details\n\nCreate
 d by: Book by Michael Stewart\, music by Charles Strouse\, lyrics by Lee A
 dams\n\nDirector: Zachary Hasbany\n\nLocation: Sonoma State University –
  Warren Theater\, Ives Hall\, 1801 East Cotati Ave\, Rohnert Park\, CA 949
 28\n\nPerformance dates: September 18 – October 4\, 2026\; Fridays & Sat
 urdays 7:30pm\, Sundays 2:00pm\n\nEstimated run time: 2 hours\, with one 1
 0-minute intermission\n\nRecommended for families / all ages\n\nASL-Interp
 reted Performance\n\nSunday\, September 27 at 2:00 PM\n\nThis performance 
 will feature American Sign Language \\(ASL\\) interpretation. Patrons who 
 would like seating with a clear view of the ASL interpreter can contact th
 e Box Office at \\(707\\) 763-8920 or boxoffice@cinnabartheater.org.\n\nTi
 ckets: https://ci.ovationtix.com/35211
LOCATION:Sonoma State University - Warren Auditorium
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/byebyebirdie/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
