DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T170000
UID:260925V8W4rP9DNUOdXLr4ox5Qeg
DESCRIPTION:Bank of America cardholders receive free general admission to 
 participating museums nationwide on the first full weekend of each month\;
  this month is October 3-4. \n\nAs a chill settles in the air\, Halloween
  costumes are planned\, and leaves crunch on the ground\, take a moment th
 is busy fall season to enjoy local culture! The Sonoma Valley Museum of Ar
 t has exciting exhibits including brand new installation The Real-Life Art
  History of M. Louise Stanley\, an exhibit sponsored by Bank of America th
 at celebrates a unique Bay Area Figurative artist for her wildly imaginati
 ve narratives and distinctly female perspective\, shaped by her keen obser
 vations of everyday life and setting her apart from her male contemporarie
 s. The exhibit features Sanley’s large-scale acrylic paintings\, gouache
  and watercolor works on paper\, sculptural objects\, sketchbooks\, studie
 s\, photos\, and notes from her personal archives\, showing the artist’s
  perspective across multiple media forms. \n\nBank of America Museums on 
 Us program offers FREE weekend general admission on the first full weekend
  of every month to Bank of America\, Merrill and Bank of America Private B
 ank credit and debit cardholders. All you need is your Bank of America\, M
 errill\, or Bank of America Private Bank card and picture ID for access. 
 \n\nAdditional participating museums can be found here: https://about.bank
 ofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-partner
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art
URL:https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-part
 ners
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
