BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jack London's Neighbors: The History of the Sonoma Developmental C
 enter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T113000
UID:260918vhYFUeAP_kivc--wQrk5bA
DESCRIPTION:Join historical ecologist Angela Nardo-Morgan for a look at th
 e early history of what became the Sonoma Developmental Center\, from its 
 origins in the late 19th century to its closure.\n\nPresented in partnersh
 ip with the Glen Ellen Historical Society\, the program will explore the f
 ounding of the institution at Eldridge in 1891\, its development and chang
 ing philosophies of care\, and the important role it played in shaping the
  surrounding Glen Ellen community. The program will also consider the broa
 der history of the area during the lifetimes of Jack and Charmian London\,
  including the institution’s proximity to London’s Beauty Ranch.\n\nNo
 te: This program focuses on the historical period of the Sonoma Developmen
 t Center up until its closure and does not cover current redevelopment pla
 ns or discussions.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/jl-sdc/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
