BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Songs of the Living Earth
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T153000
UID:260910iGIZlW3nzE6RV5GT-hHCtA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an unforgettable evening of music\, community\, an
 d celebration as the internationally acclaimed band Curawaka travels from 
 Europe for a rare Northern California performance in Sebastopol.\n\nRooted
  in the wisdom traditions of the Earth\, Curawaka's music weaves together 
 ancestral songs\, indigenous languages\, and contemporary artistry into an
  experience that invites us to remember our deep connection with nature\, 
 one another\, and the sacred.\n\nThe day begins with an opening circle to 
 bring our hearts and minds into coherence through collective song. We will
  have opening acts with Madhu Anziani and AeaLuz\, each bringing their own
  unique expression of devotional music and heartfelt artistry.\n\nThe jour
 ney then continues with Jens Jarvie\, offering songs born through years of
  ceremony\, prayer\, and deep listening. Accompanied by his band\, Jens in
 vites the audience into an uplifting experience of liberation songs and so
 ulful storytelling\, creating a bridge that leads us beautifully into the 
 night's headlining performance.\n\nThe evening culminates with the headlin
 ing act\, Curawaka\, whose music has touched hearts around the world throu
 gh its joyful celebration of life\, indigenous wisdom\, and our sacred rel
 ationship with the living Earth.\n\nThis is more than a concert\, it is a 
 woven prayer for the healing and wellbeing of all life everywhere. It is a
 n invitation to gather and come together in community\, to sing\, dance\, 
 listen\, celebrate\, and remember what it feels like to be fully alive.\n\
 nTogether we'll create an evening of beauty\, connection\, and inspiration
  that feeds the soil of our lives and  helps us to walk in a good way reme
 mbering our relationship to the great mystery and all that lives and breat
 hes through us as the infinite expression of consciousness into being. \n\
 nWe look forward to welcoming you!!
LOCATION:Sebastopol Community Cultural Center
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108739342?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sambada
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T150000
UID:260910gpF6Bj1ts0GNqSuQjhf74w
DESCRIPTION:While Brazilian natives Papiba Godinho and Dandha da Hora brin
 g their profound knowledge and respect for the roots of afro-brazilian son
 g and dance\, the entire band has developed a type of samba-reggae-funk wi
 th a universal appeal. SambaDá musically unites the Americas\, drawing fr
 om percussion based styles of South and Central America\, and blends it wi
 th that good old funk and reggae back beat so familiar to crowds of North 
 America.  For over ten years\, SambaDá has been mixing contemporary sound
 s with the roots of brazilian culture. Papiba is a master of Capoeira\, an
  Afro Brazilian martial art form created by Brazilian slaves\, which draws
  on music and acrobatic movements. Dandha was born into the rich Afro Braz
 ilian traditions of Salvador\, Bahia and the Carnival Group Ile Aiye\, and
  started her dancing career at age 6. Ile Aiye has been in the forefront o
 f Civil Rights in Brazil\, promoting equality and justice\, and is widely 
 recognized as the first Afro Brazilian BLOCO or group to perform in Brazil
 's notorious Carnival celebrations.  The other members of SambaDá come fr
 om a wide range of styles\, generations and sensibilities. What unites thi
 s band from such diverse backgrounds is a magic that can be felt by both t
 he band and the audience. SambaDá brings joy to each performance\, and ke
 eps their fans asking for more!! SambaDá musically unites the Americas\, 
 drawing from percussion-based styles of South and Central American samba a
 nd salsa\, and blending them with the funk!
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1039986822?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
