BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Children's Jamboree & Marketplace
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T140000
UID:260906Usl7XRIE0kuQtQjGybulSA
DESCRIPTION:2026 Children's Jamboree & Marketplace - Come Grow\, Learn\, P
 lay\, and Shop with Us!\n\nThis fun\, free event for children and adults i
 s Sunday\, October 11 from 11 a.m. to 2 p.m. at Nokhnoma Teaching and Demo
 nstration Garden in Santa Rosa.\n\nActivities for children will include it
 ems they can make and take home such as corn husk dolls\, sun catchers\, g
 ratitude banners\, seed pots\, garden art rocks\, and more! ﻿ ﻿\n\nMar
 ketplace will feature an assortment of 4-inch and 1-gallon succulents\, su
 cculent containers\, succulent topped pumpkins in assorted sizes\, small a
 nd medium wreaths crafted with flora\, cones and/or succulents\, oyster sh
 ell succulents and decoupage oyster shell ornaments\, beaded light catcher
 s\, and gardening books. All proceeds benefit the UC Master Gardener Progr
 am of Sonoma County. Cash\, checks and credit cards accepted.\n\nInformati
 on tables will be staffed with Sonoma County Master Gardener volunteers wh
 o will share home gardening information\, answer your home gardening-relat
 ed questions and provide information about our programs and projects.\n\nP
 artner organizations on site will include the Girl Scouts\, Sonoma County 
 Bee Association\, Children's Museum of Sonoma County\, Master Food Preserv
 ers\, Zero Waste\, Sonoma County 4-H\, and others.\n\nRegister to attend: 
 Go to https://tinyurl.com/5dk8nw7r or sonomamg.ucanr.edu/ Upcoming Events
  to complete your registration. After registering\, you will receive a con
 firmation email containing information about attending the event.\n\nGener
 al information\n\nADA-compliant porta potty on site.\n\nADA parking will b
 e available.\n\nWater available for filling water bottles.\n\nWear comfort
 able\, closed-toe shoes suitable for walking on unpaved\, uneven paths\n\n
 Bring a hat if desired.\n\nNo animals allowed\, except trained service dog
 s.\n\nFood and beverages will not be available\, bring your own snacks or 
 picnic lunch.
LOCATION:Nokhnoma Teaching and Demonstration Garden
URL:https://tinyurl.com/5dk8nw7r
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SugarShuttle: Sugarloaf ↔ Hood Mtn\, Los Alamos Rd
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T115500
UID:260903TQQJTv975EK982F8t55QOw
DESCRIPTION:**How it works**: Every hour\, our Shuttle will leave
  from either Sugarloaf Ridge State Park's Visitor Center\, making
  a brief stop at the Goodspeed parking lot\, or Hood Mountain 
 Regional Park’s Los Alamos Rd parking lot. Make a reservation 
 to ride to the other end of the trail and begin your hike\, o
 r hike and ride back. We recommend riding first and hiking back
  to your car afterward—no worries about how long you take to
  finish your adventure. The hike should take 4 to 5 hours depe
 nding on your pace\; the distance is about 7.5 miles one-way wi
 th approximately 2\,500ft of elevation gain. \n\nBring at least 6
 4 oz of water\, sun protection (the majority of the trail is e
 xposed)\, a good paper map (some of the trail signs on Hood Mt
 n Regional Park are still damaged from the 2020 wildfire and tr
 ails might not be well marked)\, and if desired\, hiking poles\,
  a lunch\, and a friend.\n\nIf you are riding from Sugarloaf\, 
 the Goodspeed lot fills up quickly. If it is full\, please park
  at the main lot and pick up the shuttle at the Visitor Cente
 r (you will have to hike a mile back to the main lot from th
 e bottom of the canyon/Goodspeed lot). Remember\, the Hood Mounta
 in pick-up is at the end of Los Alamos Road: 3000 Los Alamos 
 Rd\, Santa Rosa\, CA\, 94509. Los Alamos Rd is a windy\, narrow
 \, sometimes one-lane\, 5-mile road without cell reception—allow
  time to get to the lot (NOT the Pythian Rd lot). Please note
  there are currently no restrooms\, water\, or cell service at 
 this trailhead.  \n\n**Registration is required as there is only
  space for 6 riders at a time**\, but you can ride on a spac
 e-available basis as well. There is no charge for the ride\, th
 e $10 reservation fee is refunded on site the day of the event
 \, unless you choose to donate it to keep this service running.
  **Dogs and bikes are not allowed in the shuttle or on Goodspe
 ed Trail** (the State Park portion of the hiking route). Parking
  fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026octsatshuttle
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
