BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Karen Gebbia Kids Event Meet & Greet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T150000
UID:260924qhN9K9eOy0y05BrcOZW69g
DESCRIPTION:Join us to celebrate Karen Gebbia's new picture book about wai
 ting patiently! And we'll be serving sweet tea as only our manager can mak
 e it\, so you won't have to wait for that!\n\nSo\, what's it about?\n\nCha
 rlotte wants to wait patiently. She really does. But waiting is hard\, esp
 ecially on a stifling Maryland morning\, when her t-shirt feels like a hot
 \, heavy blanket\, and she can't think of anything but Nana's cold\, sweet
 \, lemony\, real iced tea.\n\nThere are so many steps to Nana's secret rec
 ipe tea! Steeping\, sugaring\, cooling . . . baking muffins to go with it!
  Nana tells her to find something useful to do while she waits\, so Charlo
 tte sweeps\, and swings\, and snaps pillowcases\, but it still isn't ready
 !\n\nCharlotte has to find more things to do to pass the time\, and soon s
 he finds that a day spent waiting can be a day spent enjoying the slower m
 oments. Sometimes the sweetest things in life are the things we have to wa
 it for\, and learning to savor them slowly is a joy all its own. Included 
 is a reader's note for adults on helping kids learn how to wait and a secr
 et recipe to try at home.\n\nAuthor info!\n\nKaren Gebbia is a children's 
 book writer and naturalist based in California. Before writing for childre
 n\, Karen spent two decades writing\, publishing\, editing\, and teaching 
 scholarly writing.
LOCATION:Copperfield's Books- Petaluma
URL:https://copperfieldsbooks.com/event/2026-10-17/karen-gebbia-meet-greet
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:1st Annual First Responder Car Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T150000
UID:260924lEMS24ifoEKqebCd45evEA
DESCRIPTION:CALLING ALL FIRST RESPONDERS & CAR ENTHUSIASTS!    \n\nJoi
 n First Responders Resiliency\, Inc.® for the 2026 First Responders Ca
 r Show — a day of incredible cars\, community\, connection\, and suppor
 t for those who serve.\n\n Saturday\, October 17\, 2026  10:00 AM – 3:
 00 PM\n\n First Responder Resiliency Center 1475 W. Sierra Ave.\, Cotati\
 , CA 94931\n\n General Admission: FREE  Vehicle Registration: $35\n\n B
 RING YOUR CAR\n\nHave a vehicle you’re proud of? We want to see it! Regi
 ster your vehicle for $35\, which includes your vehicle entry and two ad
 missions\, including the driver.\n\n COME ENJOY THE SHOW\n\nGeneral admis
 sion is FREE! Bring your family\, check out the cars\, connect with fell
 ow first responders and community members\, and spend the day supporting a
  great cause.\n\n SUPPORT FIRST RESPONDERS\n\nProceeds benefit First Res
 ponders Resiliency\, Inc.®\, helping provide first responders and their f
 amilies with training\, tools\, resources\, and support to better manage t
 he cumulative effects of stress and trauma throughout their careers and be
 yond.\n\nPlease note: This is a private event for first responders and t
 heir families. Guests bringing anyone under 18 must complete a Release of 
 Liability Waiver.\n\n Bring the crew.  Bring the car.  Bring the family
 .\n\nShow up for those who show up for us.
LOCATION:The First Responders Resiliency Center
URL:https://resiliency1st.org/event/carshow101726/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
