BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Migrations: Birds and Words on Oona-pa'is (Sonoma Mountain)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T110000
UID:2609184dq05QdHIEKa28Y1WFPN5w
DESCRIPTION:Migrations have been integral to wild and human lives on Oona-
 pa’is for millennia. Following favorable climate\, familial ties\, and f
 ood availability is necessary to a community’s survival and healthy dive
 rsity.\n\nIn mid to late October\, species of birds who have summered else
 where arrive to forage the mountain’s forests and stream corridors. Vari
 ed and hermit thrushes\, fox sparrows\, and Townsend’s warblers are amon
 g the fall visitors and returning residents to Oona-pa’is.\n\nJoin Rebec
 ca Lawton\, long-time guide\, author\, and scientist\, for a bird walk on 
 Oona-pa’is \\(Sonoma Mountain\\).\n\nSpend the morning looking and liste
 ning for new avian arrivals\, like the Townsend’s warbler \\(pictured\\)
 . Keeping a list for submittal to eBird\, adding group sightings to databa
 ses used by scientists who research the mysteries of migrations\, the grou
 p will explore how valuable migrants are to local ecosystems and neighborh
 oods.\n\nThis will be a relaxed\, slow-paced walk suitable for ages 12 and
  up. The total distance will depend on the bird activity encountered\, but
  plan for approximately 1–3 miles round trip.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/migrationsbirdsandwords-october-2026
 /
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
